 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# NameError in prepare_token_request method\n\nI'm trying to use the OAuth2 client to prepare a token request, but I'm getting a NameError. It seems like the `prepare_token_request` method is trying to call a function that doesn't exist.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\nHere's a simple example that reproduces the issue:\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2 import Client\n\nclient = Client(client_id='my_client_id')\nclient.code = 'authorization_code'\nclient.redirect_url = 'https://example.com/callback'\n\n# This fails\ntoken_url, headers, body = client.prepare_token_request(\n    token_url='https://example.com/token',\n    authorization_response='https://example.com/callback?code=authorization_code',\n)\n```\n\n## Error message\n\nWhen running the above code, I get the following error:\n\n```\nNameError: name 'prepare_token_request' is not defined\n```\n\nIt looks like the method is trying to call a function named `prepare_token_request` but this function isn't defined anywhere. I checked the code and it seems like it should be calling `self.prepare_request_body` instead, which is what it was doing before.\n\nThis is breaking my OAuth2 flow as I can't exchange the authorization code for a token anymore.\n</issue>\n",
